there's a bear chasing me  oh  okay  hey you have to leave now you have to  leave now you're supposed to leave  goodbye  what is up everyone mad luigi here and  today i want to preach the good news of  the seamless co-op mod for eldon ring if  you don't know recently a mod called  seamless co-op was released in beta on  nexus mods it allows players to engage  in co-op in elden ring without the  normal limitations of summoning and  re-summoning this mod lets you join your  friend's game and play continuously  until you choose to leave dying doesn't  disconnect you killing the area boss  doesn't disconnect you and you can even  fast travel all together the mod is easy  to install and essentially works by  having you play in offline mode and  disabling anti-cheat once downloaded and  running the mod allows players to  connect directly to each other  peer-to-peer it doesn't use fromsoft  servers so there should be minimal  possibility of getting banned or  penalized by fromsoft but of course  don't solely take my word for it and  read for yourself what the mod does on  its download page to make sure that you  are okay with using it and to make sure  that you're using it correctly to avoid  penalty but also allow me to say this  mod is an amazing amount of fun the  normal co-op of from software games  achieves a certain feeling but it's  totally different to being able to  continually progress through the game  with friends in a seamless fashion and  yes each player can progress normally  with the mod each player can upgrade  weapons level up stats and collect loot  all from the same world if you've played  other instanced rpgs with a more  integrated co-op system this is pretty  similar not to mention that the mod is  made impressively well it was only just  released in beta but for a mod of this  kind where i would expect a whole host  of desync issues i was amazed by how  well everything flowed and by the  quality of the mod aspects from new  items to activate the new co-op mode to  integrated animations such as the one to  turn pvp on and here we see another  radical change that this mod brings the  ability to continually pvp with your  friends friendly fire can be turned on  or off through a new item and with the  feature you can battle your friends  without needing to re-summon them or  simply fight through the game world with  realistic damage to each other turned on  demanding that you play carefully so as  to not kill each other while you fight  the monsters of the lands between and i  can't tell you how refreshing it is to  be able to play the game with friends  and not have to fret with constant  re-summoning and switching between  worlds i can only speak for myself but  the standard way of multiplayer  implementation in these games while  definitely achieving its own kind of  experience can get pretty exhausting  when i want to just play continuously  with my friends for those of you who  might not have heard the story the  inspiration for the style of multiplayer  in fromsoft games came from a personal  event in game director hidetaka  miyazaki's life according to a eurogamer  article released in the wake of demon  souls the drop dropout co-op style was  inspired by a time when miyazaki and  some others got their cars stuck on a  snowy hill some strangers in the car  behind him helped pushed his car to get  it unstuck and going again as miyazaki  tells it i couldn't stop the car to say  thanks to the people who gave me a shove  i'd have just got stuck again if i'd  stopped on the way back home i wondered  whether the last person in the line had  made it home and thought that i would  probably never meet the people who had  helped me i thought that maybe if we'd  met in another place we'd become friends  or maybe we'd just fight you could  probably call it a connection of mutual  assistance between transient people  this event supposedly created the  transient co-op system we find in the  souls games and an elden ring where  anonymous players drop in help you  overcome a boss or defeat an invader or  invade you and then leave just as  quickly the anonymous aid of traditional  phantoms is good to create a certain  feeling for the player progressing  through the world but it also demands a  set of game mechanics that can be pretty  frustrating for friends just trying to  enjoy the game as a shared experience  basically the thing from software is  trying to achieve through their  multiplayer is great at delivering an  experience like the one miyazaki had in  his snow-stuck car but it is not  tailored to friends trying to  consistently co-opt together while there  is plenty of discussion that could be  had about fromsoft's intentions and game  design when it comes to multiplayer that  conversation really only has to be had  if we want from soft to change how  they're doing things  this mod doesn't demand that it just  gives players the opportunity to  experience the game in a different way  and at this point most people using the  mod are probably going to be people who  have already played through the game so  it isn't changing most people's first  experience with the story or the game as  a whole with that in mind i can't  recommend this mod highly enough to  anyone who has already played through  the game and would like some variation  or to players who would like to play  with their friends in a much more  seamless and fluid experience one  drawback to note is that because the  game is operating in offline mode  without connection to fromsoft servers  there are no invasions which is too bad  and even though there is additional  scaling for the enemy health and  difficulty it still has the opportunity  to turn pretty easy with multiple people  especially if everyone is riding around  on torrent or using op builds  fortunately the mod plays in offline and  is compatible with other mods so extra  difficulty can be added if needed  through that avenue you could also opt  to always keep pvp on for an extra  dosing of difficulty it's harder to spam  kill every enemy if you have to worry  about your attacks hitting your fellow  tarnished this is something i've been  having a lot of fun with so if it seems  like a fit for you i hope it can deliver  a similar experience if you're looking  for variety simple and straightforward  fun with friends or an easily repeatable  pvp opportunity like dark souls 3's  arenas this mod is a great option maybe  one day fromsoft will give us some elden  ring arenas in the coliseums maybe  through dlc but until then i'll be  pvping my friends this way where i only  have to wait for them to respawn out of  grace before we can fight again a much  more pleasant experience than  re-summoning and re-summoning and  re-summoning and as i also said there's  a good discussion to be had about what  kinds of changes should be made to the  actual multiplayer of elton ring but  i'll save that for another video this  one will just be a psa about a fun  alternative well i hope you've enjoyed  the video and be sure to subscribe if  you want to see more elden ring content  on lore game mechanics and more feel  free to talk in the comments about your  thoughts on fromsoft multiplayer whether  or not you've used and enjoyed this mod  and what other game mechanics and lore  you'd like to see discussed on my  channel you can also share what you  think about these videos that are more  centered on game mechanics than lore  most of my stuff is lore but branching  out into these game mechanic videos i'd  be interested to see what people have to  say i'll be away from making videos for  a little bit after this one comes out so  there will be some time before i release  another lore deep dive more time for all  of you to get your suggestions in the  comments in the meantime i have a few  videos like this one scheduled to  release somewhat weekly well thank you  for watching and i'll see you in the  next video peace  all right

